cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Poros in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Poros: Large-Model Fine-Tuning on Consumer GPUs"
abstract: >-
  Poros fine-tunes LoRA adapters on language models larger than the GPU's
  memory: the frozen NF4 base waits in host RAM and streams through the GPU one
  block of layers at a time, and the backward pass recomputes each block. Runs
  go from the command line or step by step through a Python Run API, with SFT,
  DPO and other objectives as recipes, mixture-of-experts models with their
  experts in host RAM or on an SSD store, and Apple silicon Macs.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jeffrey
    family-names: Tigres
    affiliation: "Caistro Labs"
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Caistro-Labs/poros"
keywords:
  - QLoRA
  - LoRA
  - fine-tuning
  - large-language-models
  - memory-efficient-training
  - blockwise-residency
